       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Dose:** 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for ibuprofen in adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. For OTC use it is 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks:** At this level the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events goes up a lot. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily:** 3,200 mg/day, the usual maximum, for example for inflammatory conditions.\n- **400\u2013800 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours:** typical for pain or fever.\n- **1600 mg per day in total:** for example 400 mg four times daily, or 800 mg twice daily. This may be what was meant if the 1600 mg was a daily total.\n\nTell me which dose you want, or confirm that you really mean 1600 mg four times daily and give the clinical reason. I'll enter the order once that's settled."
      }
